cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AeroSysProp, please cite the software using the metadata below,
  and cite the original publications for each method you use (listed in
  THIRD_PARTY.md and in each method card).
title: AeroSysProp
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-06
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24013620
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: https://github.com/environmental-ai-systems/AeroSysProp
abstract: >-
  AeroSysProp is a Python library and web application for predicting
  thermophysical properties of organic compounds relevant to atmospheric
  aerosol research from SMILES strings. It provides group contribution
  estimates of boiling points, vapour pressures, critical properties and
  liquid densities, AIOMFAC activity coefficients for mixtures with
  inorganic ions, diagnostics for unassigned functional groups, versioned
  method cards with parameter fingerprints, provenance records for batch
  runs, and an interface for AI agents through the Model Context Protocol.
keywords:
  - atmospheric aerosol
  - group contribution
  - vapour pressure
  - activity coefficients
  - AIOMFAC
  - SMILES
